{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "My Sweet! Housemate",
    "steam_appid": 3100210,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3100210/extras/24f54d3f146d15ac5883d405750891b8.avif?t=1751647872\" width=657 height=258 /></span><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3100210/extras/1f6507a8cbeb38508b9c50fd1a11a52a.avif?t=1751647872\" width=601 height=174 /></span>My Sweet Housemate is an interactive visual novel style game that puts you into the shoes of a homeless adult struggling to find affordable housing in America. You're hit with a stroke of good - or maybe bad - luck when you finally find a totally not suspicious rental listing for a room in an apartment. The only catch is that your new landlord, Seung-min, seems to have something off about him.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3100210/extras/d0eb8f3931ecc4a4eaee609d290b08e7.avif?t=1751647872\" width=619 height=509 /></span>  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Find out more in this deliciously horrifying experience!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3100210/extras/a0bd76fab7516abf74e36e1c649b9c6f.avif?t=1751647872\" width=601 height=174 /></span>The game features:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Character customisation that includes name, pronouns and voice</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Choice, exploration and mini-game based gameplay</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple endings, replayability and in-game achievements</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1-2 hours of comedy-filled gameplay</p></li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3100210/extras/24f54d3f146d15ac5883d405750891b8.avif?t=1751647872\" width=657 height=258 /></span><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3100210/extras/1f6507a8cbeb38508b9c50fd1a11a52a.avif?t=1751647872\" width=601 height=174 /></span>My Sweet Housemate is an interactive visual novel style game that puts you into the shoes of a homeless adult struggling to find affordable housing in America. You're hit with a stroke of good - or maybe bad - luck when you finally find a totally not suspicious rental listing for a room in an apartment. The only catch is that your new landlord, Seung-min, seems to have something off about him.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3100210/extras/d0eb8f3931ecc4a4eaee609d290b08e7.avif?t=1751647872\" width=619 height=509 /></span>  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Find out more in this deliciously horrifying experience!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3100210/extras/a0bd76fab7516abf74e36e1c649b9c6f.avif?t=1751647872\" width=601 height=174 /></span>The game features:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Character customisation that includes name, pronouns and voice</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Choice, exploration and mini-game based gameplay</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple endings, replayability and in-game achievements</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1-2 hours of comedy-filled gameplay</p></li></ul>",
    "short_description": "Faced with the cruel and harsh reality of homelessness, you seek out affordable housing in your area. Luckily, it seems you've found the perfect rental, but something is very off about your landlord...",
